Job Description 1
Responsibilities:
- Perform 3D finite element modeling, structural analysis, and design for high-rise, commercial, and residential building projects.
- Design reinforced concrete (RCC) structural elements including foundations, columns, shear walls, transfer slabs, and beams.
- Analyze lateral load-resisting systems under wind and seismic loading using dynamic response spectrum and equivalent static methods.
- Coordinate with architectural, MEP, geotechnical, and construction teams to resolve spatial clashes and incorporate design constraints.
- Prepare, review, and approve structural calculation packages, detailed design drawings, and bar bending schedules (BBS).
- Conduct structural peer reviews and ensure compliance with local building bye-laws and international design standards.
Minimum Qualifications:
- Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Civil or Structural Engineering.
- 4+ years of experience in structural design of reinforced concrete and steel structures.
- Strong proficiency in structural analysis tools such as ETABS, SAP2000, SAFE, and STAAD.Pro.
- In-depth understanding of building codes such as ACI 318, AISC 360, ASCE 7, IBC, IS 456, IS 1893, and IS 875.
- Working knowledge of AutoCAD and Revit Structure for BIM-based project delivery.
- Strong grasp of structural mechanics, load path determination, and lateral stability.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Professional Engineer (PE) or Chartered Engineer (CEng) license.
- Experience with performance-based seismic design (PBD) and non-linear pushover analysis using PERFORM-3D.
- Familiarity with post-tensioned (PT) slab design using RAM Concept or ADAPT-Builder.
- Experience with wind tunnel testing data integration into finite element models.

