Job Description 4
Responsibilities:
- Perform structural design and detailing of precast and prestressed concrete components (hollow-core slabs, precast columns, spandrel beams, load-bearing insulated wall panels).
- Analyze structural performance during demolding, lifting, transportation, and temporary erection stages to prevent handling cracking and overstressing.
- Design standard and customized precast connections, including corbels, grouted splice sleeves, base shoe connections, weld plates, and loop ties.
- Build parametric 3D structural BIM models and oversee the generation of automated shop fabrication drawings and rebar bending schedules.
- Coordinate with precast manufacturing plant production teams and field erection crews to resolve site queries (RFIs) and non-conformance reports.
Minimum Qualifications:
- Bachelor’s degree in Civil/Structural Engineering.
- 3+ years of experience in precast/prestressed concrete engineering and modular building systems.
- Proficiency with structural engineering software such as Tekla Structures, ETABS, Tedds, or Mathcad.
- Deep familiarity with precast standards such as the PCI Design Handbook, ACI 318, Eurocode 2 (EN 1992-1-1), and relevant local precast guidelines.
- Strong comprehension of crane rigging mechanics, dynamic amplification factors during transport, and temporary bracing requirements.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Hands-on experience developing custom Tekla components or parametric Grasshopper/Revit scripts for precast automation.
- Familiarity with cast-in-place and precast hybrid structural framing systems.
- Experience with modular volumetric steel/concrete pod design.

