Job Description 5
Responsibilities:
- Conduct structural capacity audits, condition assessments, and forensic investigations for aging, fire-damaged, or seismically vulnerable structures.
- Interpret Non-Destructive Testing (NDT) data including rebound hammer, ultrasonic pulse velocity (UPV), core compression tests, and cover meter scans.
- Perform advanced non-linear static (pushover) and dynamic time-history analyses to determine collapse mechanisms and seismic demand/capacity ratios.
- Design structural strengthening and seismic retrofit interventions utilizing carbon fiber-reinforced polymers (CFRP), steel jacketing, concrete sectional enlargement, and supplemental damping systems.
- Prepare comprehensive structural forensic evaluation reports, retrofit calculation notes, technical specifications, and repair BOQs.
- Perform soil-structure interaction and differential settlement evaluations for foundations exhibiting distress.
Minimum Qualifications:
- Master’s or Bachelor’s degree in Structural Engineering.
- 6+ years of experience in structural forensics, seismic evaluation, and repair/rehabilitation design.
- Proficiency in non-linear analysis software such as PERFORM-3D, SeismoStruct, SAP2000, or DIANA FEA.
- Expert knowledge of evaluation and repair codes including ASCE 41, FEMA P-58, ACI 562 (Concrete Repair Code), and ACI 440 (FRP Strengthening).
- Strong understanding of concrete degradation mechanisms and structural cracking typologies.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Proven experience designing base isolation systems (lead-rubber bearings, friction pendulum bearings) or tuned mass dampers.
- Active participation in structural forensic societies or published structural failure investigation studies.
- Experience on-site supervising carbon fiber wrapping and epoxy pressure injection repairs.

