Job Description 7
Responsibilities:
- Lead the structural design and analysis of deep foundation systems, earth retaining structures, and underground basement facilities.
- Perform soil-structure interaction (SSI) modeling for high-rise mat foundations, piled rafts, diaphragm walls (slurry walls), and secant/tangent pile walls.
- Design permanent and temporary excavation support systems including ground anchors, tie-backs, strut-waler systems, and soil nail walls.
- Calculate soil lateral earth pressures, hydrostatic uplift forces, settlement profiles, and heave under varied groundwater regimes.
- Coordinate with geotechnical specialists to interpret geotechnical investigation reports, borehole logs, and pressuremeter test data.
- Prepare technical design calculation packages, instrumentation monitoring plans, and excavation sequence drawings.
Minimum Qualifications:
- Master’s or Bachelor’s degree in Geotechnical/Structural Engineering.
- 5+ years of design experience in deep basements, retaining walls, and heavy foundation systems.
- High proficiency in geotechnical and structural software such as PLAXIS 2D/3D, GeoStudio (SLOPE/W, SEEP/W), WALLAP, SAFE, and SAP2000.
- In-depth understanding of codes such as ACI 318, Eurocode 7 (EN 1997), FHWA deep foundation manuals, CIRIA C760, and BS 8004.
- Strong understanding of geotechnical-structural interface mechanisms, consolidation settlement, and lateral soil-pile response ($p-y$ curves).
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience with seismic soil-structure interaction and liquefaction mitigation design.
- Hands-on experience interpreting geotechnical instrumentation data (inclinometers, piezometers, settlement markers).
- Familiarity with marine quay wall, cofferdam, or cut-and-cover tunnel box design.

