Job Description 8
Responsibilities:
- Perform structural engineering, finite element analysis, and detailing for building façade systems, curtain walls, skylights, and bespoke architectural envelopes.
- Design structural aluminum extrusions, stainless steel fittings, cable nets, point-supported glass (spider fittings), and unitized curtain wall mullions/transoms.
- Calculate wind suction/pressure distributions, thermal expansion movements, seismic building inter-story drift accommodation, and dead/live load deflections.
- Perform structural glass stress checks and post-breakage capacity assessments for laminated, tempered, and insulated glass units (IGUs).
- Design anchor brackets, embedment channels, and structural fastenings connecting façade assemblies to the main concrete/steel building frame.
- Review façade fabrication shop drawings, thermal/condensation analysis reports, and witness visual/structural performance mock-up (PMU) testing in accredited laboratories.
Minimum Qualifications:
- Bachelor’s degree in Civil, Structural, or Façade Engineering.
- 3–6 years of experience in structural design of building envelopes and curtain wall systems.
- Proficiency in structural and finite element analysis software such as SJ MEPLA, Strand7, RFEM/RSTAB, SAP2000, or Mathcad.
- Deep familiarity with façade design standards including ASTM E1300, AAMA standards, CWCT guidelines, ASCE 7, and Eurocode 9 (EN 1999) / Eurocode 11 (Structural Glass).
- Solid grasp of structural glass mechanics, polymer interlayer shear transfer behavior, and aluminum alloy limit-state design.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience with complex parametric envelope design using Rhino, Grasshopper, and Revit.
- Knowledge of blast-resistant glazing design according to GSA/DOD criteria.
- Experience with façade dynamic seismic drift mock-up testing and wind tunnel pressure-tap data mapping.

