Job Description 11
Responsibilities:
- Perform 3D finite element analysis and structural design for post-tensioned (PT) concrete building systems, including bonded and unbonded post-tensioned flat plates, banded beams, and transfer girders.
- Calculate initial and long-term prestress losses (elastic shortening, creep, shrinkage, steel relaxation, and friction/wobble effects).
- Perform detailed serviceability checks including cracked section analysis, punching shear capacity evaluations at column-slab junctions, and long-term deflection control.
- Design post-tensioning anchorages, bursting reinforcement, pocket formers, and tendon profile geometry (parabolic, harped, and cantilever).
- Coordinate tendon layouts with MEP openings, core walls, slab depressions, and edge form details to eliminate physical routing clashes.
- Review and approve post-tensioning shop drawings, elongation calculation sheets, and stressing logs submitted by PT specialist contractors.
Minimum Qualifications:
- Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Civil or Structural Engineering.
- 4+ years of focused structural design experience in post-tensioned and prestressed concrete buildings.
- High proficiency in post-tensioning design software such as RAM Concept, ADAPT-Builder, SAFE, or RAPT.
- Strong knowledge of building design codes and PT standards including ACI 318, PTI (Post-Tensioning Institute) DC10.5, Eurocode 2 (EN 1992-1-1), and IS 1343.
- Solid understanding of load balancing methods, equivalent frame methods, and hyperstatic (secondary) moment calculations.
- Experience with AutoCAD and Revit Structure for PT tendon profiling and rebar detailing.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience in design of heavy post-tensioned transfer plates and deep transfer girders in high-rise towers.
- On-site experience witnessing tendon stressing, gauge calibration, elongation measurement, and duct grouting operations.
- Professional Engineer (PE) or Structural Engineer (SE) license.

