Job Description 13
Responsibilities:
- Perform structural design, modeling, and detailing for water and wastewater treatment structures, environmental holding tanks, reservoirs, and pump stations.
- Design liquid-containing reinforced concrete structures (circular prestressed tanks, rectangular aeration basins, clarifiers, and digestion chambers).
- Execute severe environmental serviceability limit state calculations, including crack width limitation control, direct tension stress checks, and thermal shrinkage cracking minimization.
- Perform structural buoyancy and hydrostatic uplift checks under fluctuating groundwater levels, specifying uplift anchors and ballast slabs.
- Design watertight construction joints, expansion joints, PVC/hydrophilic waterstops, and chemical-resistant concrete cover schemes.
- Coordinate with process, mechanical piping, and environmental engineering teams for equipment anchorage, pipe thrust blocks, and dynamic pump loads.
Minimum Qualifications:
- Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Civil/Structural Engineering.
- 3–7 years of structural design experience in environmental, water/wastewater, or heavy civil treatment facilities.
- Proficiency in structural analysis programs such as STAAD.Pro, ETABS, SAFE, or Robot Structural Analysis.
- In-depth understanding of water-retaining structural codes including ACI 350 / ACI 350.3 (Seismic Design of Liquid-Containing Concrete Structures), Eurocode 2 Part 3 (EN 1992-3), BS 8007, and IS 3370.
- Strong understanding of concrete durability in aggressive chemical/sulfate environments and corrosion prevention technologies.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience designing wire-wound circular prestressed concrete water tanks according to AWWA D110.
- Familiarity with seismic hydrodynamic convective (sloshing) and impulsive fluid-structure interaction analysis.
- Experience with 3D BIM coordination in Autodesk Revit or Bentley OpenBuildings.

