Job Description 15
Responsibilities:
- Perform structural analysis, condition assessment, dynamic load evaluation, and detailed design for railway infrastructure, including rail bridges, track overpasses, passenger station canopies, and pedestrian footbridges.
- Execute structural modeling under heavy freight axle loading, high-speed rail dynamic train-track-bridge interaction, and centrifugal forces.
- Evaluate fatigue damage, cyclic stress ranges, and structural vibration limits for welded steel and composite rail superstructures.
- Design railway substructure elements, crash protection collision walls, impact-resistant piers, and electrification mast (OHE) support foundations.
- Perform track-structure interaction (TSI) and rail expansion analysis to calculate longitudinal rail stresses due to temperature and bridge deck flexure.
- Coordinate with track alignment, signaling, geotechnical, and railway operations teams to schedule construction staging within rail possession windows.
