- Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Civil/Structural Engineering with emphasis on Transportation/Railway Infrastructure.
- 4–8 years of experience in structural design of railway bridges and heavy rail transit facilities.
- Proficiency in bridge analysis tools such as MIDAS Civil, LUSAS Bridge, RM Bridge, or STAAD.Pro.
- Deep familiarity with railway structural design standards including AREMA (Manual for Railway Engineering), UIC Codes (e.g., UIC 774-3 for TSI), Eurocode 1 Part 2 (EN 1991-2), and IRS (Indian Railway Standards).
- Strong comprehension of bridge dynamic amplification factors, resonance risk at critical train speeds, and derailment load provisions.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience with high-speed rail (HSR) bridge design and dynamic bridge deck acceleration limit checks (<3.5 m/s²).
- Familiarity with accelerated bridge construction (ABC) methods for rapid rail replacement (jack-in bridges, SPMT installations).
- Knowledge of railway station BIM coordination and asset management systems.

