Job Description 16
Responsibilities:
- Perform finite element analysis and structural design for nuclear power plant containment structures, auxiliary buildings, and safety-related civil infrastructure.
- Execute seismic Soil-Structure Interaction (SSI) modeling using substructure and direct finite element techniques under Safe Shutdown Earthquake (SSE) and Operating Basis Earthquake (OBE) conditions.
- Design heavily reinforced and prestressed post-tensioned concrete containment vessels (PCCV) and biological radiation shielding walls.
- Evaluate structural members under extreme design basis events including aircraft impact, missile impact (tornado/turbine missiles), pipe whip, and internal accidental overpressure.
- Perform high-temperature thermal stress analysis and crack width control calculations to maintain airtight and leak-tight boundaries.
- Coordinate with nuclear licensing bodies, safety review committees, and mechanical equipment qualification teams.
