- Master’s or PhD degree in Structural or Civil Engineering.
- 5+ years of dedicated structural design experience in nuclear facilities or safety-critical power structures.
- Proficiency in advanced finite element and SSI software such as SASSI, ANSYS, ABAQUS, SAP2000, or GT STRUDL.
- Comprehensive knowledge of nuclear design codes including ACI 349 (Code Requirements for Nuclear Safety-Related Concrete Structures), ACI 359 / ASME Section III Division 2, AISC N690, ASCE 4-16 (Seismic Analysis of Safety-Related Nuclear Structures), and ASCE 43-05.
- Deep expertise in non-linear dynamic time-history analysis, impulse loading, and concrete confinement under extreme shear and compression.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience with Small Modular Reactor (SMR) or Advanced Reactor structural layout design.
- Direct experience in probabilistic seismic hazard analysis (PSHA) and structural fragility evaluation.
- Active professional registration (PE / SE) and security clearance suitability.

