Job Description 17
Responsibilities:
- Perform structural analysis, modeling, and detailed engineering for telecommunication infrastructure, including self-supporting lattice towers, guyed masts, monopoles, and rooftop antenna mounts.
- Analyze structures under severe wind loading, gust factors, radial ice accumulation, seismic events, and mount-specific antenna drag forces.
- Execute tower structural capacity audits, existing member overstress checks, and reinforcement design (member split-pipe jacketing, diagonal bracing replacement, guy wire retensioning).
- Design foundation systems for tall tower infrastructure, including pad-and-pier foundations, drilled micropiles, rock anchors, and guy anchor blocks.
- Perform twist, sway, and tilt serviceability deflection checks to ensure operational beam alignment for high-frequency microwave and 5G cellular equipment.
- Review climbing safety systems, fall-arrest ladders, platform grates, and feedline cable ladder attachments.
