- Bachelor’s degree in Civil or Structural Engineering.
- 3–6 years of experience in structural design and evaluation of telecom towers and wireless structures.
- Hands-on expertise in tower analysis software such as TnxTower (formerly RISA Tower), OpenTower, Tower Numerics, or STAAD.Pro.
- In-depth understanding of telecommunications structural codes including ANSI/TIA-222 (Revision G/H), Eurocode 3 Part 3-1 (EN 1993-3-1), and ASCE 7.
- Solid understanding of bolted joint slippage, cold-formed angle member buckling, and guy cable non-linear catenary behavior.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience coordinating drone-based LiDAR tower mapping and structural inspection audits.
- Familiarity with rooftop ballast mount analysis and structural framing verification over existing building roofs.
- Experience with foundation anchor rod pull-out and corrosion remediation techniques.

