Job Description 18
Responsibilities:
- Perform computational structural engineering, advanced wind engineering analysis, and high-rise dynamic optimization for supertall towers and complex architectural landmarks.
- Coordinate with wind tunnel testing laboratories to interpret High-Frequency Force Balance (HFFB) and High-Frequency Pressure Integration (HFPI) data.
- Model and optimize lateral drift, torsional velocity, across-wind vortex shedding, and aerodynamic mitigation geometries (building corner chamfers, setbacks, porosity).
- Design and integrate dynamic damping systems including Tuned Mass Dampers (TMD), Tuned Liquid Column Dampers (TLCD), and distributed viscous dampers.
- Evaluate building acceleration metrics against international human comfort criteria (ISO 10137, AIJ guidelines) for wind-induced floor vibrations.
- Perform structural topology optimization and finite element member resizing to achieve target stiffness while reducing overall structural embodied carbon.
