- Master’s or PhD degree in Structural Engineering, Wind Engineering, or Structural Dynamics.
- 5+ years of experience in structural design of supertall buildings (200m+) or slender dynamic structures.
- High proficiency in ETABS, SAP2000, Strand7, and MATLAB / Python for custom dynamic data processing.
- Comprehensive knowledge of wind loading and dynamics codes including ASCE 7 (Chapter 26–31), ISO 4354, Eurocode 1 Part 1-4 (EN 1991-1-4), and CTBUH Tall Building Guidelines.
- Strong mathematical foundation in random vibration theory, modal analysis, spectral density functions, and aeroelastic instability phenomena (flutter, galloping).
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience with automated structural optimization workflows using Grasshopper, Karamba3D, and Python scripting.
- Published technical contributions in tall building lateral systems (mega-columns, outriggers, diagrids).
- Professional Engineer (PE) or Chartered Structural Engineer (MIStructE) credential.

