Job Description 19
Responsibilities:
- Perform structural analysis, modeling, and detailed design for modular volumetric building units and offsite prefabricated building structures (steel-chassis and hybrid concrete-timber pods).
- Design multi-story stacking connections, inter-module corner-block connectors, horizontal tying mechanisms, and foundation anchorage interfaces.
- Execute structural checks for temporary loading regimes encountered during factory demolding, bridge crane lifting, flatbed transport, and on-site crane hook lifting.
- Perform global lateral stability analyses for high-stack modular buildings resisting wind and seismic lateral shear through integrated core walls or localized inter-unit moment frames.
- Design cold-formed and structural hollow section (HSS) floor and ceiling chassis systems to meet stringent deflection and footfall vibration criteria.
- Coordinate with manufacturing production engineers, MEP modular routing specialists, and factory QA/QC inspectors to optimize Design for Manufacturing and Assembly (DfMA).
