- Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Civil, Structural, or Architectural Engineering.
- 3–7 years of experience in structural design with a dedicated focus on modular volumetric or offsite construction systems.
- Proficiency in finite element modeling programs such as Tekla Structures, ETABS, SAP2000, Robot Structural Analysis, or IDEA StatiCa.
- Strong knowledge of building design specifications including AISC 360, AISI S100, ACI 318, Eurocode 3, and national modular building guidelines.
- Solid understanding of dimensional manufacturing tolerances, field connection clearances, and progressive collapse prevention in volumetric assemblies.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience with parametric modeling and automation plugins (Revit API, Dynamo, Grasshopper).
- Knowledge of acoustic bridging and structural thermal break detailing in modular inter-unit connections.
- Hands-on experience with modular module prototype testing (rack testing, lift test certification).

