- Perform structural fire engineering, thermal-mechanical finite element modeling, and performance-based structural fire safety design for complex buildings and infrastructure.
- Model realistic fire curves (parametric fires, localized fire plumes, zone models) and heat transfer regimes through structural concrete, steel, composite, and mass timber elements.
- Evaluate temperature-dependent non-linear material degradation, reduction in mechanical yield strength, thermal expansion restraint forces, and thermal bowing stresses.
- Determine the fire resistance ratings and specify structural passive fire protection (PFP) systems including intumescent coatings, cementitious sprays, and board encasement.
- Execute finite element structural response modeling under full burnout fire scenarios to prevent progressive collapse and ensure structural compartmentalization integrity.
- Coordinate with fire safety engineers, architectural egress planners, and building authorities to defend performance-based fire engineering submissions.
Minimum Qualifications:
- Master’s or PhD degree in Structural Engineering, Fire Safety Engineering, or Civil Engineering.
- 4–8 years of experience in structural fire safety engineering or thermal-structural finite element modeling.
- High proficiency in advanced thermal and structural finite element software such as SAFIR, ANSYS, ABAQUS, LS-DYNA, or Vulcan.
- Deep understanding of structural fire standards including Eurocode 1 Part 1-2 (EN 1991-1-2: Actions on structures exposed to fire), Eurocode 2/3/4/5 fire parts, ASCE/SEI 7 / SFPE Engineering Guide to Performance-Based Fire Protection, and ACI 216.1.
- Strong knowledge of heat conduction, convection, radiation boundary interactions, and thermo-plasticity in structural systems.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience coupling computational fluid dynamics (CFD) fire models (e.g., FDS - Fire Dynamics Simulator) with structural finite element models.
- Active involvement in professional technical committees (SFPE, ASCE Fire Protection Committee, or fib).
- Professional Engineer (PE) or Chartered Engineer (CEng) registration.

