Job Description 39
Responsibilities:
- Perform finite element analysis, dynamic structural modeling, and detailed engineering for heavy industrial containment structures, chimneys, stacks, and cooling towers.
- Design tall reinforced concrete industrial chimneys and natural draft hyperbola cooling towers subjected to high wind suction, aerodynamic resonance, and thermal gradients.
- Design self-supporting and guyed industrial steel exhaust stacks, flare booms, and flue gas ducting systems in compliance with vibration and vortex shedding standards.
- Evaluate aerodynamic across-wind vortex excitation, ovaling buckling modes, and design aerodynamic helical strakes or tuned mass damping devices.
- Design heavy foundation systems, including annular ring foundations, deep piled circular caps, and high-temperature refractory lining support brackets.
- Coordinate with process engineering, flue gas treatment specialists, and mechanical piping stress teams.
Minimum Qualifications:
- Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Civil or Structural Engineering.
- 4–8 years of experience in structural design of tall industrial structures, cooling towers, chimneys, or stacks.
- High proficiency in structural analysis tools such as STAAD.Pro, SAP2000, ANSYS, or RFEM.
- Solid knowledge of industrial chimney and cooling tower standards including ACI 307 (Design and Construction of Reinforced Concrete Chimneys), ASME STS-1 (Steel Stacks), VGB-R 610 (Cooling Towers), CICIND Model Codes, and BS 4076.
- Strong understanding of aeroelastic stability, shell buckling under wind depression, and high-temperature thermal stresses.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience with flue gas acid condensation corrosion mitigation and refractory brick lining design.
- Familiarity with dynamic vibration measurement and resonant frequency validation in operational industrial stacks.
- Professional Engineer (PE) license.

