Job Description 40
Responsibilities:
- Perform structural analysis, structural acoustic decoupling modeling, and detailed engineering for performing arts centers, concert halls, broadcast studios, and vibration-isolated auditoriums.
- Design heavy reinforced concrete and structural steel "box-in-box" isolated acoustic enclosures, floating floors, and decoupled structural boundary walls.
- Design high-performance elastomeric and helical steel spring isolation systems to mitigate structure-borne ground vibration and low-frequency structure-borne noise from adjacent subways and railways.
- Perform dynamic finite element frequency-response modeling to evaluate natural frequencies, transfer functions, and vibration transmission insertion loss across building isolators.
- Design long-span column-free auditorium roof trusses, acoustic shell suspension grids, theatrical catwalk systems, and heavy rigging fly-tower structures.
- Coordinate closely with acoustic consultants, theater planners, architectural interior specialists, and MEP noise control engineers.
Minimum Qualifications:
- Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Civil, Structural, or Architectural Engineering.
- 4–8 years of structural design experience with exposure to performing arts centers, vibration-isolated facilities, or complex architectural structures.
- High proficiency in finite element modeling software such as SAP2000, ETABS, ANSYS, or Strand7.
- Strong knowledge of building design standards including AISC 360, ACI 318, ASCE 7, IBC, and acoustic vibration criteria (NC / RC curves, ASHRAE guidelines).
- Deep comprehension of structural dynamic isolation theory, impedance mismatching, transmissibility ratios, and dynamic footfall-induced acoustic emissions.
Preferred Qualifications:
- Experience designing theater fly-towers and rigging grid iron structures according to ANSI E1.21 / ESTA technical standards.
- Familiarity with on-site vibration measurement testing (accelerometers, spectrum analyzers) and isolation bearing static/dynamic deflection verification.
- Professional Engineer (PE) or Structural Engineer (SE) credential.

